# Tidy URLs for the pages people are most likely to type or share.
#
# These are 301s rather than 200 rewrites on purpose. A rewrite serves the same
# page at two addresses, which leaves Google consolidating duplicates for us and
# reporting each one as "Alternate page with proper canonical tag". A redirect
# settles it at the server instead, so there is one address per page.
/bring-a-mate         /bring-a-mate.html        301
/moving-up            /moving-up.html           301
/dofe                 /dofe.html                301
/join                 /join.html                301
